{
  "name": "Webhook reliability: retry with exponential backoff",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 944,
        "content": "## Retry with exponential backoff\nReceives a JSON POST and forwards it to your target URL. Failures are retried with a doubling delay plus jitter. After the last attempt the payload goes to the dead-letter queue workflow.\n\n### How it works\n1. The webhook answers at once with n8n's immediate acknowledgement. The caller does not get the delivery result.\n2. `Call Target` POSTs the payload. Network errors, 408, 429 and 5xx are retried; other 4xx go straight to the dead-letter queue.\n3. Delay = `base_delay_seconds * 2^(attempt-1)` plus jitter (up to 25% of the base), capped at 300 s.\n4. When `max_attempts` is used up, `Send to Dead Letter Queue` posts the payload to the other workflow. If that call fails, the payload can be lost.\n\n### Setup\n1. Before activating, enable Header Auth on the Webhook node. These webhooks are unauthenticated by default.\n2. In `Config`, set `target_url` to your endpoint and `dlq_url` to the dead-letter queue workflow's webhook URL (both are `example.invalid` placeholders and will not work until replaced). Optionally change `base_delay_seconds` and `max_attempts`.\n3. If you also protect the dead-letter queue webhook: `Send to Dead Letter Queue` sends no auth header. Select the same n8n credential on that node, or the hand-off fails.\n\nTested headless on n8n 2.35.7 (2026-10-13); not yet imported through the editor UI by a human. Test steps and limits: README.md and TESTING.md at https://github.com/claude-farm-hq/n8n-webhook-reliability\n\nWritten by an AI agent working for Martin Minkov, who owns and is accountable for it.\nBuilt and operated by Martin Minkov with AI agents. Contact: mminkov@aubian.net\nLicense: MIT."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b",
      "name": "Section: Receive and configure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        608,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 352,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Receive and configure\nThe webhook answers at once. `Config` holds your URLs and retry limits."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
      "name": "Section: Call the target",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1008,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 512,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Call the target\nPOSTs the payload. A 2xx response counts as delivered."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d",
      "name": "Section: Retry or hand off",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1008,
        352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 512,
        "height": 464,
        "content": "## Retry or hand off\nOn failure: work out the delay, wait, call again. After the last attempt, send the payload to the dead-letter queue."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
